<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><p:notes xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name="" /><p:cNvGrpSpPr /><p:nvPr /></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Slide Image Placeholder 1" /><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1" xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldImg" idx="0" /></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr /></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Notes Placeholder 2" /><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1" xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="1" /></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr /><p:txBody><a:bodyPr xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /><a:lstStyle xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>This is the live demo slide.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>The user workflow has four steps. First, the user chooses the model method in the sidebar, either XGBoost or SARIMA. Second, the user sets the forecast horizon from 1 to 26 weeks. Third, Streamlit sends the request to the Flask API. Fourth, the app displays the forecast as both a chart and a table.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>For the demo, I would first open the Streamlit app:</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>https://fuel-price-streamlit-oluqiqxkmq-uw.a.run.app</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>Then I would choose XGBoost, set the horizon to 8 weeks, and click "Get forecast." I would point out that the chart is not just computed inside Streamlit. Streamlit is calling the deployed API service.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>To show the API directly, I can open the health endpoint:</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>https://fuel-price-api-oluqiqxkmq-uw.a.run.app/health</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>That returns JSON showing the API is alive and lists the supported methods.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>Then I can show a prediction request with this command:</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>curl -X POST https://fuel-price-api-oluqiqxkmq-uw.a.run.app/predict \</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>  -d '{"horizon":8,"method":"xgboost"}'</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>The response includes the method, horizon, last historical period, validation metrics, and a list of forecasted dates and prices. This demonstrates the core app/API interaction required by the final project.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:r><a:t>If the live demo is slow, I would still explain the flow clearly: the dashboard is the front end, Flask is the model service, and /predict is the contract between them.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Slide Number Placeholder 3" /><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1" xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldNum" idx="5" /></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr /><p:txBody><a:bodyPr xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /><a:lstStyle xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /><a:p xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" /></p:clrMapOvr></p:notes>